module examples.err_layout_offset_outside

# plans/M7.md item B, 02-language.md §13: "`@offset(n)` — field offset
# inside a `@layout` declaration." On an ordinary struct there is no byte
# layout for it to name, so it is rejected rather than ignored — an
# ignored `@offset` is a author's belief about the bytes that the compiler
# never checked.

struct Header:
    @offset(0x004) sector: u64
